Subject: [PATCH 10757/11362] A document/YAML task-count divergence cost 3 of 4
 tasks in milestone 602

exp6874 is clean and its gate failed honestly on v602_document_yaml_parity: the
milestone document describes 11 tasks, experiment_range 6874 to 6884, while the
activated YAML holds 4. Two dependent checks failed with it. exp6875, 6876 and 6877
then GATE_BLOCKed in a chain on that root failure -- three of the milestone's four
tasks.

The guard is not the problem here. exp6874 caught a real inconsistency between two
descriptions of the same milestone and refused to certify it, and the cascade is the
dependency machinery working once the root gate fails. The divergence is the defect.

The obvious suspect was this morning's replan, since 602 was refused by the
exclusion-manifest guard at 11:10 and re-planned before activating at 11:20. That
does not survive checking: the log holds 5 such replans across .576, .583, .593,
.597 and .602, and exactly one artifact in results/ has ever failed a
document_yaml_parity check. So replanning does not generally cause this and
something specific to 602 does.

Not diagnosed, and the entry says so. Both planner runs logged 4 tasks proposed, so
the 11 did not come from trimming a larger plan. The range 6874 to 6884 is exactly
11 consecutive ids, which suggests the document reserves an id range rather than
counting tasks -- a hypothesis, not a finding, since the document generator was not
read. Filed so the next occurrence starts from a reference point.

